<title>USA: Illinois Central agreement ratified by BMWE.</title>
<headline>Illinois Central agreement ratified by BMWE.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brotherhood of Maintenance of Way Employees (BMWE) said its members ratified a five-year agreement reached earlier this month with llinois Central Railroad, a unit of Illinois Central Corp.</p>
<p>The BWME represents about 450 employees throughout Illinois Central's system who construct and maintain track, bridges, buildings and repair track equipment.</p>
<p>The agreement settles wage and work rule issues through 1999. Illinois Central said this is the ninth union to ratify a local agreement with the company. Together, the nine unions represent about 60 percent of all Illinois Central employees covered by bargaining agreements.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
